 "notes": "The old cases/ep516-517_furinkazan.json file compressed a four-murder-plus-one-attempt serial-killing arc (patterned after Takeda Shingen's 'Furinkazan' banner maxim) down to a single simplified victim (Ayaka) and named Tatsue Torada as murderer with a 'Forest, Nagano' location and a generic rifle/dying-message pair of objects -- this rebuild confirms Tatsue IS the correct primary culprit (matches transcript: she shot Kai Kuroto's horse six years ago causing his death, then killed Yoshirou, Kouji and Ayaka to silence the four people who separately caused Kai's fall via a firework prank, and attempted to kill Akira as the final 'fire' target) but the old file entirely missed that the fourth on-screen death (Shigetsugu, initially theorized mid-episode as the serial killer who then died by suicide) was actually a SEPARATE murder committed by Torada Yui (Yoshirou's widow, a former police officer who infiltrated the family to investigate Kai's death and took her own revenge on Shigetsugu via an email-and-electrified-train-wire trick) -- a second, distinct culprit the old file has no trace of. The old file's dying-message decode ('Aokage'/dark horse pointing at the rider of a black horse) is accurate but was actually an eyeshadow smear on Ayaka's hand, not a message 'written in eyeshadow'. case_type: murder (serial, two culprits: one primary serial murderer + one separate revenge killing exploiting the same pattern).",
